{"name":"Blue Nude","hex":"#29518c","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"nude","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Without clothing or other covering of the skin; without clothing on the genitals or female nipples.","Of a color (such as beige or tan) that evokes bare flesh."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A painting, sculpture, photograph or other artwork or mass-media-reproduced image depicting one or more human figure(s) in a state of near or total undress.","The state of total nudity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nude"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Nude (Souvenir de Biskra)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Nude (Souvenir of Biskra) (French: \"Nu bleu, Souvenir de Biskra\"), an early 1907 oil painting on canvas by Henri Matisse, is located at the Baltimore Museum of Art as part of the Cone Collection."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Matisse_Souvenir_de_Biskra.jpg/330px-Matisse_Souvenir_de_Biskra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Nude_(Souvenir_de_Biskra)","wikidata":"Q882584"},{"title":"Blue Nudes","blocks":[{"text":"The Blue Nudes is a series of collages, and related color lithographs, by Henri Matisse, made from paper cut-outs depicting nude figures in various positions. Restricted by his physical condition after his surgery for stomach cancer, Matisse began creating art by cutting and painting sheets of paper by hand; these Matisse viewed as independent artworks in their own right. The Blue Nudes refers also to the editioned multiples based on the cut-outs. Matisse supervised the creation of these lithographs until his death in 1954."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/78/Blue_Nudes_Henri_Matisse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Nudes","wikidata":"Q119188441"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Matisse_Souvenir_de_Biskra.jpg/500px-Matisse_Souvenir_de_Biskra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Matisse_Souvenir_de_Biskra.jpg/1280px-Matisse_Souvenir_de_Biskra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Matisse_Souvenir_de_Biskra.jpg/500px-Matisse_Souvenir_de_Biskra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMatisse_Souvenir_de_Biskra.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Henri_Matisse%2C_1906-07%2C_Nu_couch%C3%A9%2C_I_%28Reclining_Nude%2C_I%29%2C_exhibited_at_Montross_Gallery%2C_New_York%2C_1915.jpg/500px-Henri_Matisse%2C_1906-07%2C_Nu_couch%C3%A9%2C_I_%28Reclining_Nude%2C_I%29%2C_exhibited_at_Montross_Gallery%2C_New_York%2C_1915.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Henri_Matisse%2C_1906-07%2C_Nu_couch%C3%A9%2C_I_%28Reclining_Nude%2C_I%29%2C_exhibited_at_Montross_Gallery%2C_New_York%2C_1915.jpg/1280px-Henri_Matisse%2C_1906-07%2C_Nu_couch%C3%A9%2C_I_%28Reclining_Nude%2C_I%29%2C_exhibited_at_Montross_Gallery%2C_New_York%2C_1915.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Henri_Matisse%2C_1906-07%2C_Nu_couch%C3%A9%2C_I_%28Reclining_Nude%2C_I%29%2C_exhibited_at_Montross_Gallery%2C_New_York%2C_1915.jpg/500px-Henri_Matisse%2C_1906-07%2C_Nu_couch%C3%A9%2C_I_%28Reclining_Nude%2C_I%29%2C_exhibited_at_Montross_Gallery%2C_New_York%2C_1915.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Henri Matisse, 1906–07, Nu couché, I, Aurore (Reclining Nude, I), exhibited at Montross Gallery, New York, 1915","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHenri_Matisse%2C_1906-07%2C_Nu_couch%C3%A9%2C_I_(Reclining_Nude%2C_I)%2C_exhibited_at_Montross_Gallery%2C_New_York%2C_1915.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/78/Blue_Nudes_Henri_Matisse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/78/Blue_Nudes_Henri_Matisse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_Nudes_Henri_Matisse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://th